These are the models for the mount kits, kindly provided by the brains behind Boost Fabrication - thank you guys! They sell a fabricated, powder coated mount kit off the shelf here:-
https://www.boostfabrication.co.uk/product-page/preorder-mr2-mk3-to-1-8t-vag-engine-mounts

The drawings/models are here for all though, they can be made by companies such as Fractory etc, or your local laser cutting and folding firm.

They are designed to fit the 2wd Gearbox from a MK2 TT / Golf Gti etc.
Known as the 02Q Gearbox - e.g. 02Q300045A

The left hand mount fits the 2wd gearbox alloy bridge mount only, part number 1K0199117 which I call "the banana mount", this a banana mount will fit the 4wd gearbox but you need to drill and tap the holes that are unfinished in the gearbox by VAG - the marks and locations are there though.

The rear diff mount requires 2 holes in the gearbox drilling and tapping, there is a video on youtube about it. (pending upload) These are p[artially drilled, they just need upsizing to 8mm then tapping to M10 etc.

There is also a rear diff mount designed to fit the rear 4wd Gearbox, using the cheap alloy block found on ebay with title "Golf R32 VR6 6 speed 02M gearbox conversion for 2WD front-wheel drive AL0090" that is about £85 - it requires 4 holes drilling and tapping in the alloy block. There is a video here on youtube about it. (pending upload)


